anglion"},{"label":"B","text":"Soma"},{"label":"C","text":"Astrocyte"},{"label":"D","text":"Nissl"},{"label":"E","text":"Terminal bouton"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2624f1a7d82c529d78248133d5b40dbded293844"},{"id":"q-4d0f32ebd313","stem":"Where is the ependyma found?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lining ventricles"},{"label":"B","text":"Lining spinal canal"},{"label":"C","text":"Covering the brain"},{"label":"D","text":"Covering the spinal cord"},{"label":"E","text":"Both a and b The ependyma lines the ventricles and spinal canal."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"020570807511e60f5124f01ad488c236405cf818"},{"id":"q-a308952a6f65","stem":"Which type of neuron is most abundant?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sensory neurons"},{"label":"B","text":"Motor neurons"},{"label":"C","text":"Interneurons"},{"label":"D","text":"Both a and b"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above The vast majority of neurons are interneurons."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d0e24eb143dbf1d056e60ba3b320d7f670ff00a2"},{"id":"q-a6e98f74839d","stem":"What surrounds a bundle of nerve fibers?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Neurium"},{"label":"B","text":"Perineurium"},{"label":"C","text":"Epineurium"},{"label":"D","text":"Endoneurium"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f0cd13ad04b0fa1f1c95a1d5b428220a39d8cc2b"},{"id":"q-4307f02f247c","stem":"Which meninx covers the brain intimately?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dura mater"},{"label":"B","text":"Arachnoid"},{"label":"C","text":"Pia mater"},{"label":"D","text":"Both a and b"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"51d3aad51727faef5b98f7dc7e88fa91988fa3a8"},{"id":"q-1547efbdc1e7","stem":"Which of the following is the largest neuroglia cell?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Astrocytes"},{"label":"B","text":"Ependymal cells"},{"label":"C","text":"Oligodendrocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"Microglia"},{"label":"E","text":"Schwann cells Neuroglia are the supporting cells of the central nervous system. Sometimes, neuroglia called glial cells or glia. Astrocytes, ependymal cells, oligodendrocytes, and microglia are all neuroglia. Of the neuroglia cells, astrocytes are the most abundant and the largest. These are star shaped cells involved in the blood brain barrier. Ependymal cells line the ventricles and spinal canal. Oligodendrocytes form myelin in the central nervous system. Microglia are the central nervous system macrophages. Schwann cells are seen in the peripheral nervous system and are not considered neuroglia. Schwann cells are responsible for the myelination of neurons in the peripheral nervous system."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d4c5c0404f7cd153780f109c1db9aafc754def0c"},{"id":"q-10d0b689afdb","stem":"Which of the following is NOT considered neuroglia?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Astrocytes"},{"label":"B","text":"Ependymal cells"},{"label":"C","text":"Oligodendrocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"Microglia"},{"label":"E","text":"Schwann cells Neuroglia are the supporting cells of the central nervous system. Sometimes, neuroglia called glial cells or glia. Astrocytes, ependymal cells, oligodendrocytes, and microglia are all neuroglia. Of the neuroglia cells, astrocytes are the most abundant and the largest. These are star shaped cells involved in the blood brain barrier. Ependymal cells line the ventricles and spinal canal. Oligodendrocytes form myelin in the central nervous system. Microglia are the central nervous system macrophages. Schwann cells are seen in the peripheral nervous system and are not considered neuroglia. Schwann cells are responsible for the myelination of neurons in the peripheral nervous system."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2a87a4e726064816d54960a8d710325e876c8add"},{"id":"q-38c8c5edb0fc","stem":"What is the innervation of an eccrine sweat gland?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cholinergic; parasympathetic"},{"label":"B","text":"Cholinergic; sympathetic"},{"label":"C","text":"Adrenergic; parasympathetic"},{"label":"D","text":"Adrenergic; sympathetic"},{"label":"E","text":"Cholinergic; motor Eccrine sweat glands are innervated by the sympathetic nervous system."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"7de50b1ca8787d12b486a9712590c24907d4a80d"},{"id":"q-1f8fc612e801","stem":"What is the innervation of an apocrine sweat gland?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cholinergic; parasympathetic"},{"label":"B","text":"Cholinergic; sympathetic"},{"label":"C","text":"Adrenergic; parasympathetic"},{"label":"D","text":"Adrenergic; sympathetic"},{"label":"E","text":"Cholinergic; motor Apocrine sweat glands are innervated by the sympathetic nervous system."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"52a613a75d258f44a77de1c4209ddef802757f87"},{"id":"q-e6c2e6b7060f","stem":"What are the supporting cells in the central nervous system called?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Schwann cells"},{"label":"B","text":"Basket cells"},{"label":"C","text":"Ganglion"},{"label":"D","text":"Neuroglia"},{"label":"E","text":"Satellite cells"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"pu