},{"label":"C","text":"It contains the perihilar lymph nodes"},{"label":"D","text":"The oesophagus is 25cm in length"},{"label":"E","text":"The descending aorta commences at the lower level of T4 vertebra"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-434873fef85c","stem":"Which is true of the sternum?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jugular notch lies at the level of T4"},{"label":"B","text":"2nd costal cartilage articulates separately with the manubrium and the body of the sternum"},{"label":"C","text":"sternohyoid attaches to the manubrium, below the 1st costal cartilage"},{"label":"D","text":"interclavicular ligament makes no attachment to the sternum"},{"label":"E","text":"posterior surface of the manubrium is completely covered with pleura"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1412c7f319b2","stem":"Which is not a true muscle attachment to the ribs?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pectoralis mnior – anterior surface of ribs 3-5"},{"label":"B","text":"Serratus posterior superior – lateral to the angle of ribs 2-5"},{"label":"C","text":"Internal oblique – inner surface of last 6 costal cartilages"},{"label":"D","text":"Levator costae – lateral to tubercle, on upper border"},{"label":"E","text":"Rectus abdominus – anterior surface of 5th-7th cartilages"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-215b8d87f8f1","stem":"Which is not a feature of a typical rib?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Medial facet of the tubercle faces backwards"},{"label":"B","text":"Angle is the most posterior point"},{"label":"C","text":"Necks are all of equal length"},{"label":"D","text":"There are 3 costotransverse ligaments"},{"label":"E","text":"Intraarticular ligament attaches from horizontal ridge on the head to the intervertebral disc"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f180abcecdda5d12067049ba0fa2101d7d87a2a8"},{"id":"q-0506cedeee24","stem":"Which is true of the first rib?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":n