rs the point of confluence of the left internal jugular and axillary vein"},{"label":"C","text":"Receives the left jugular and subclavian lymph trunks"},{"label":"D","text":"Receives lymph from the right thoracic wall"},{"label":"E","text":"Passes in front of the oesophagus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b561301c492aed63a59947f1c8267cd4a3432ba1"},{"id":"q-40f442fd6bc1","stem":"The phrenic nerve","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Attempts to reach the midline at all levels"},{"label":"B","text":"Is solely motor"},{"label":"C","text":"Lies in front of the lung root"},{"label":"D","text":"Passes through the diaphragm at T12"},{"label":"E","text":"Splits into two main branches on the undersurface of the diaphragm"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3f6269c4300bd8dfb84a001e54764c192e3d0f7f"},{"id":"q-2f3cade2c9d9","stem":"In the chest wall","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The neurovascular bundle lies between the external and internal intercostals"},{"label":"B","text":"The transverses muscle lies between the internal and external intercostals"},{"label":"C","text":"The intercostal artery lies netween the nerve and vein"},{"label":"D","text":"The intercostal artery is more superficial than the vein"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6c5963fa6e75d42a3025216974069ed7e419af1b"},{"id":"q-cff2bac26598","stem":"The oesophageal opening in the diaphragm is at","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Diaphragm","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"T6"},{"label":"B","text":"T8"},{"label":"C","text":"T10"},{"label":"D","text":"T12"},{"label":"E","text":"L1"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-471428833d8a","stem":"The most superficial structure in the thoracic inlet is the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vagus nerve"},{"label":"B","text":"Superior vena cava"},{"label":"C","text":"Right subclavian artery"},{"label":"D","text":"Left subclavian artery"},{"label":"E","text":"Thoracic duct"}],"pri