surface markings of the lung and pleura","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The border of the lung lies two ribs below the pleural reflection"},{"label":"B","text":"The hilum of the lungs lie at the level of T10 verterbra"},{"label":"C","text":"The oblique fissure follows the line of T10 vertebra"},{"label":"D","text":"The oblique fissure follows the line of the 5th rib"},{"label":"E","text":"The horizontal fissure meets the oblique fissure in the left midaxillary line"},{"label":"F","text":"The lower border of the lung lies at the level of the sixth rib in the midaxillary line"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"c693065a5f29f0f2beef05a3b6520b3fd6644aca"},{"id":"q-91f19e303d73","stem":"Thoracic skeleton","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the function of the ribs is primarily to protect the thoracic contents"},{"label":"B","text":"each rib articulates with its own thoracic vertebra and the one above"},{"label":"C","text":"the tubercle of a typical rib has two facets, the lateral facet being non-articular"},{"label":"D","text":"the 2nd to 7th sternocostal joints are synovial type, each with a single cavity"},{"label":"E","text":"the body of the sternum usually fuses with the manubrium with advancing age"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-32cbc13033be","stem":"With respect to the thoracic wall, which is TRUE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"intercostal and lumbar arteries pass forward in the neurovascular plane between internal and external oblique"},{"label":"B","text":"lymphatic drainage above the umbilicus drains posteriorly to the scapular (post) group of axillary nodes"},{"label":"C","text":"division of a single intercostal nerve causes anaesthesia in its supply area"},{"label":"D","text":"the thoracoepigastric vein unites the internal thoracic vein and the superficial epigastric vein – connecting IVC and SUC"},{"label":"E","text":"venous return follows intercostal and lumbar arteries only"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-31d3518bae7b","stem":"The oesophagus passes through the diaphragm at the level of T10 vertebra. It is accompanied by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Diaphragm","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"right phrenic nerve"},{"label":"B","text":"left phrenic nerve"},{"label":"C","text":"oesophageal branch of the right gastric artery"},{"label":"D","text":"vagal trunks"},{"label":"E","text":"hemiazygous vein"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fa0cccdd2537","stem":"The aorta passes through the diaphragm at the level of T12. It is accompanied by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Diaphragm","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"azygous vein"},{"label":"B","text":"thoracic duct"},{"label":"C","text":"hemiazygous vein"},{"label":"D","text":"a and b correct"},{"label":"E","text":"a, b and c correct"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-aa317557fcd3","stem":"The IVC passes through the diaphragm at the level of T8, which is TRUE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Diaphragm","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"this occurs to the left of the midline behind the 7th costal cartilage"},{"label":"B","text":"the left phrenic nerve accompanies it"},{"label":"C","text":"this occurs behind the 8th right costal cartilage"},{"label":"D","text":"the right phrenic nerve accompanies it"},{"label":"E","text":"it passes between the muscular levels of the diaphragm"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"10367b0b621ce0279e76dfbae7e80c9f3284fb74"},{"id":"q-41ed43501a8b","stem":"Accessory muscles of inspiration include all EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"scalene muscles"},{"label":"B","text":"latissimus dorsi"},{"label":"C","text":"sternocleidomastoid"},{"label":"D","text":"quadratus lumborum"},{"label":"E","text":"erector spinae"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7c8f17555239","stem":"With respect to the superior mediastinum, which is FALSE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Mediastin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the trachea is separated from the apex of the left lung by the left common carotid and left subclavian"},{"label":"B","text":"the SUC and brachiocephalic veins lie anterior to the brachiocephalic trunk"},{"label":"C","text":"the vagus nerve (right) lies medial to the right common carotid artery"},{"label":"D","text":"the trachea bifurcates at the lower limit of the superior mediastinum"},{"label":"E","text":"the thymus lies behind the manubrium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2d750a576d78","stem":"With respect to the mediastinum","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Mediastin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the vagus nerves pass in front of the lung roots"},{"label":"B","text":"the phrenic nerves pass behind the lung roots"},{"label":"C","text":"the vagus nerves pass behind the lung roots"},{"label":"D","text":"the left phrenic passes anterior to the left bronchus and exits the diaphragm through the IVC opening"},{"label":"E","text":"the right recurrent laryngeal nerve hooks around the ligamentum arteriosum"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-d9eb0e0a428a","stem":"With respect to the cardiac plexuses","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the superficial plexus lies to the right of the ligamentum arteriosum, in front of the tracheal bifurcation, behind the aortic arch"},{"label":"B","text":"the deep plexus is smaller and lies in front of the ligamentum arteriosum"},{"label":"C","text":"the plexuses consist only of sympathetic and parasympathetic fibres"},{"label":"D","text":"pain fibres run with sympathetic nerves → sympathetic ganglia (3 cervical and upper 4-5 thoracic ganglia of both sides)"},{"label":"E","text":"sympathetic fibres accelerate the heart and constrict the coronary arteries"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2a1d8558de48","stem":"With respect to the heart","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the inferior (diaphragmatic) surface is made up of one third right ventricle and two thirds left ventricle, separated by the posterior interventricular branch of the left coronary artery"},{"label":"B","text":"the right border of the heart extends from the lower border of the right 3rd costal cartilage to the lower border of the right 6th costal cartilage"},{"label":"C","text":"the posterior surface (base) consists almost entirely of the left atrium receiving the three pulmonary veins"},{"label":"D","text":"the left border consists of the left ventricle only"},{"label":"E","text":"the right border consists mostly of the right atrium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8f5b48ca1b4b","stem":"All but which of the following are tributaries of the coronary sinus of the heart?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the anterior cardiac vein"},{"label":"B","text":"the great cardiac vein"},{"label":"C","text":"the middle cardiac vein"},{"label":"D","text":"the oblique vein (of the LA)"},{"label":"E","text":"the posterior vein of the LV"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"eee40ccbfcc4795712b27724e2c59bdaeefe1a64"},{"id":"q-eed385daa4d5","stem":"The posterior mediastinum contains all but which of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Mediastin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"thoracic aorta"},{"label":"B","text":"oesophagus"},{"label":"C","text":"accessory hemiazygous vein"},{"label":"D","text":"the azygous vein"},{"label":"E","text":"the sympathetic trunks"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"0c639830cc103e0c733c0a7e00b9ecbd09ad5c86"},{"id":"q-295634043e4a","stem":"With respect to the root of the lung","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the left pulmonary artery is longer than the right"},{"label":"B","text":"the bronchial branch to the upper lobe is separate on the left"},{"label":"C","text":"the pulmonary veins lie anterior and inferior to bronchus"},{"label":"D","text":"the pulmonary ligament connects the right and left lungs directly"},{"label":"E","text":"the pulmonary trunk divides in front of the right main bronchus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6549c9202136","stem":"The deep cardiac plexus","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"is functionally separate from the superficial cardiac plexus"},{"label":"B","text":"lies to the right of ligamentum arteriosum"},{"label":"C","text":"receives predominantly right phrenic input"},{"label":"D","text":"is posterior to the bifurcation of the trachea"},{"label":"E","text":"is smaller than the superficial cardiac plexus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b8ec1c791ba7","stem":"The abdominal inferior vena cava","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"is shorter than the abdominal aorta"},{"label":"B","text":"enters the thorax through muscular diaphragm at T8"},{"label":"C","text":"creates a groove over the quadrate lobe of liver"},{"label":"D","text":"crosses the right renal and suprarenal arteries"},{"label":"E","text":"commences in front of the right common iliac artery"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-53265445fe28","stem":"The testicular veins","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"have valves at their terminations"},{"label":"B","text":"is formed by two venae comitantes in the pelvis"},{"label":"C","text":"enter the inferior vena cava"},{"label":"D","text":"receive the suprarenal veins as tributaries"},{"label":"E","text":"none of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-048b79ccf352","stem":"Regarding the ribs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the 1st costal cartilage articulates with the manubrium by a synovial joint"},{"label":"B","text":"the radiate ligament has two bands, upper and lower"},{"label":"C","text":"the typical ribs are 3rd to 10th"},{"label":"D","text":"the groove for the subclavian artery is anterior to the scalene tubercle on the 1st rib"},{"label":"E","text":"the angle of the 2nd rib is the most posterior part of its curvature"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83ac5b1ad7e2","stem":"Regarding attachments to the thoracic cage","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"pectoralis major has slips of origin from the upper 8 costal cartilages"},{"label":"B","text":"the first digitation of serratus anterior attaches to the 1st and 2nd rib"},{"label":"C","text":"rectus abdominus is attached to the anterior surfaces of the 7th to 10th costal cartilages"},{"label":"D","text":"iliocostalis and longissimus, parts of erector spinae, are attached between the heads and tubercles of each rib"},{"label":"E","text":"serratus anterior is attached to the lower 8 ribs"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"4f006ceae29ec365bd56b103c7c655c3f98c54c4"},{"id":"q-52fdc3a6ecca","stem":"In the superior mediastinum","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Mediastin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the azygous vein arches under the right main bronchus"},{"label":"B","text":"the right brachiocephalic vein receives the thoracic duct"},{"label":"C","text":"the aortic arch is crossed on the left side by the phrenic and vagus nerves"},{"label":"D","text":"the superficial cardiac plexus contains right and left vagal and sympathetic fibres"},{"label":"E","text":"the superior vena cava receives the azygous vein at the lower border of the right 1st costal cartilage"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8c92c5821212480d2d868018f9620809c6725fef"},{"id":"q-18b1f7305073","stem":"Regarding the pericardium","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the superior vena cava does not fuse with the fibrous pericardium"},{"label":"B","text":"the transverse sinus separates the four pulmonary veins"},{"label":"C","text":"the parietal layer of the serous pericardium has no nerve supply"},{"label":"D","text":"the strong sternopericardial ligaments connect fibrous pericardium to upper/lower ends of sternum"},{"label":"E","text":"the oblique sinus permits pulsation of the left atrium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d906918254d454972016d05da47b0a40a4171c20"},{"id":"q-483c15f3720f","stem":"Regarding the gastrointestinal tract","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the oesophagus enters the abdomen at T8 level"},{"label":"B","text":"the right gastric artery is a branch of the splenic artery"},{"label":"C","text":"the hepatopancreatic ampilla opens into the horizontal part of the duodenum"},{"label":"D","text":"the taeniae coli converge at the ileocaecal valve"},{"label":"E","text":"McBurneys point is one third of the way up the oblique line that joins the right anterior superior iliac spine to the umbilicus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-68eab20dad55","stem":"The pelvic splanchnic nerves are","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"derived from S1, 2, 3, 4"},{"label":"B","text":"motor to the mm of bladder neck and anal sphincter"},{"label":"C","text":"motor to all the gut"},{"label":"D","text":"secretomotor to the gut from splenic flexure dome"},{"label":"E","text":"sympathetic nerves"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-78e83a3a6ec1","stem":"The anterior third of the serotom is supplied by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"ilioinguinal nerve"},{"label":"B","text":"sciatic nerve branches"},{"label":"C","text":"peroneal branches of the posterior femoral cutaneous nerve"},{"label":"D","text":"a branch of the pudendal nerve"},{"label":"E","text":"none of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-588f036603c1","stem":"The ureters","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"are 25cm long"},{"label":"B","text":"are crossed anteriorly by gonadal vessels"},{"label":"C","text":"leave the psoas muscle at the bifurcation of the common iliac artery"},{"label":"D","text":"are retroperitoneal"},{"label":"E","text":"all of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","short_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2fbe4f454551","stem":"Regarding intercostal blood vessels","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"in each space there are single anterior and posterior intercostal veins"},{"label":"B","text":"right sided superior intercostal vv drain into the brachiocephalic vein"},{"label":"C","text":"the second intercostal space does not contain a posterior intercostal artery"},{"label":"D","text":"all intercostal vv are branches of the descending thoracic aorta"},{"label":"E","text":"all this is clinically relevant"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"9967892360ca5fab8a06d16a573e2cb50174f255"},{"id":"q-dd2404083d0c","stem":"Regarding blood supply to the heart","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the SA nodal artery is more commonly a branch of the left coronary artery"},{"label":"B","text":"40% of hearts show “left dominance”"},{"label":"C","text":"the marginal and anterior interventricular arteries are the main branches of the left coronary artery"},{"label":"D","text":"the right coronary artery arises from the posterior aortic sinus"},{"label":"E","text":"the circumflex artery travels in the atrioventricular groove"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1f0d88d8003f","stem":"With respect to the bronchi","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the carina lies to the left of the midline"},{"label":"B","text":"the left apicoposterior bronchus of the upper lobe rises highest from the posterior surface of the lung"},{"label":"C","text":"each lung has eight segmental bronchi"},{"label":"D","text":"the left main bronchus is shorter than the right"},{"label":"E","text":"blood supply is via the pulmonary arteries"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ae13e03ab12e","stem":"The thoracic duct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"commences at L1"},{"label":"B","text":"passes through the oesophageal opening of the diaphragm (