tency is a comparative measure, refers to the different doses of two drugs that are needed to produce the same effect"},{"label":"D","text":"The ED50 is a measure of drug’s efficacy"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"newly_reasoned_provisional","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6da8ea526d01ada6aac01feec08beaa3fd453c35"},{"id":"q-a5cda7a3d74f","stem":"Give the definition for a therapeutical dose","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The amount of a substance to produce the minimal biological effect"},{"label":"B","text":"The amount of a substance to produce effects hazardous for an organism"},{"label":"C","text":"The amount of a substance to produce the required effect in most patients"},{"label":"D","text":"The amount of a substance to accelerate an increase of concentration of medicine in an organism"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d63ee5ed3dc7","stem":"Pick out the correct definition of a toxic dose","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The amount of substance to produce the minimal biological effect"},{"label":"B","text":"The amount of substance to produce effects hazardous for an organism"},{"label":"C","text":"The amount of substance to produce the necessary effect in most of patients"},{"label":"D","text":"The amount of substance to fast creation of high concentration of medicine in an organism"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f157cce6056a","stem":"Which effect may lead to toxic reactions when a drug is taken continuously or repeatedly?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Refractoriness"},{"label":"B","text":"Cumulative effect"},{"label":"C","text":"Tolerance"},{"label":"D","text":"Tachyphylaxis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6139b1f167ed","stem":"What term is used to describe a more gradual decrease in responsiveness to a drug, taking days or weeks to develop?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Refractoriness"},{"label":"B","text":"Cumulative effect"},{"label":"C","text":"Tolerance"},{"label":"D","text":"Tachyphylaxis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f547f2cace6b","stem":"What term is used to describe a decrease in responsiveness to a drug which develops in a few minutes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Refractoriness"},{"label":"B","text":"Cumulative effect"},{"label":"C","text":"Tolerance"},{"label":"D","text":"Tachyphylaxis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-11d62b8986c1","stem":"Tachyphylaxis is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A drug interaction between two similar types of drugs"},{"label":"B","text":"Very rapidly developing tolerance"},{"label":"C","text":"A decrease in responsiveness to a drug, taking days or weeks to develop"},{"label":"D","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"newly_reasoned_provisional","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-01e74f9a10a8","stem":"Drug resistance is a term used to describe the loss of effectiveness of antimicrobial or antitumour drugs. This consideration is","type":"True / False","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antimicrobial","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"True"},{"label":"B","text":"False"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bef0bab2cda5","stem":"Tolerance and drug resistance can be a consequence of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Drug dependence"},{"label":"B","text":"Increased metabolic degradation"},{"label":"C","text":"Depressed renal drug excretion"},{"label":"D","text":"Activation of a drug after hepatic first-pass"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b2843f8a2e832dc4bcf4b3b749c7e9eca7794be1"},{"id":"q-e810c1ef4412","stem":"Tolerance and drug resistance can be a consequence of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Change in receptors, loss of them or exhaustion of mediators"},{"label":"B","text":"Increased receptor sensitivity"},{"label":"C","text":"Decreased metabolic degradation"},{"label":"D","text":"Decreased renal tubular secretion"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b2843f8a2e832dc4bcf4b3b749c7e9eca7794be1"},{"id":"q-51aa516b3617","stem":"Tolerance develops because of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Diminished absorption"},{"label":"B","text":"Rapid excretion of a drug"},{"label":"C","text":"Both of the above"},{"label":"D","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-59ff3a2dc49b","stem":"Dependence is often associated with tolerance to a drug, a physical abstinence syndrome, and psychological dependence (craving). This consideration is","type":"True / False","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"True"},{"label":"B","text":"False 11"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":f